    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d8">

                <pb facs="0030" n="20" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg20"/>

                <head>Mr. Adams to Mr. Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 555.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">London,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-12-11"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 11, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Mr. Dudley, the consul at Liverpool, has
                    sent me several depositions of men who have been engaged and paid by a
                    commercial house in Liverpool to <pb facs="0031" n="21" xml:id="pg21"/> make war
                    on the United States. I have sent copies to Lord Russell, with a note dated the
                    7th instant. His lordship has acknowledged the reception of it. Copies of all
                    these papers are transmitted herewith.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES FRANCIS ADAMS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d8-a1.xml" xpointer="d8-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
